<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Crimean War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1853–1856</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Crimean War was fought from 1853 to 1856 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> and an alliance of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a>. Much of the fighting centred on the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sevastopol">Sevastopol</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>'s defeat exposed its backwardness and prompted major reforms, including the emancipation of the serfs in 1861.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/crimean-war.jpg" alt="Crimean War" width="320" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William Simpson, artist (1823-1899) E[dmond]. Morin, lithographer (1824 - 1882), working for &quot;Day &amp;amp; Son, lithrs. ... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:William_Simpson_-_Attack_on_the_Malakoff.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
